# Begin with the End in Mind: Final Project Overview

In this capstone, students design, build, and refine a complete, interactive web app for a real audience.

The project is iterative and process-oriented. It is not a single linear build or a race to add the most features.

### **Sample project**

Click around to explore the sample project. Notice the skills and features from across the units. 

<iframe src="https://amandadennard-dotcom.github.io/Unit5AIF2/ares_base_dashboard.html" width="100%" height="900" style="border:none;"></iframe>

## What success looks like

> **By the end, students will:**
> - Design a clear, engaging homepage that communicates the purpose of their project
> - Organize content into meaningful sections that support user understanding
> - Show evidence of planning and iteration by refining their design over time
> - Make intentional design decisions and clearly explain their reasoning
> - Reflect on tradeoffs and how their choices impact usability and clarity

---

## Three Key Tools

Students will show their progress and thinking using three key tools. 

- **Capstone Project Handout/ Capstone.md File**: Captures student thinking, why decisions were made, and how the system works

- **Kanban Planning Board**: Tracks tasks, priorities, and workflow (To Do, In Progress, Done)

- **The App**: The tangible product showing what was built


